WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.009 --> 00:00:09.008
Environments is where your app runs: the test site your team tries, the live site your customers use, and the computers they run on.

2
00:00:09.725 --> 00:00:14.518
Open Environments in the sidebar. Each project has its own page.

3
00:00:15.218 --> 00:00:22.064
Your app says how to start the app. DevOps has looked at the project and has a suggestion. Review it.

4
00:00:22.769 --> 00:00:28.874
Answer its question, then press Use these steps. Test copies of cards use the same steps.

5
00:00:30.398 --> 00:00:41.159
Each environment shows where it runs, its address, the version that runs, and when it updates. The test site updates by itself after each merge.

6
00:00:41.876 --> 00:00:53.238
The live site changes only when you say so. With nothing waiting, Release the newest version puts the latest approved version live. A database backup is taken first.

7
00:00:53.986 --> 00:01:03.096
Places lists the computers and servers this project uses, and what uses them. Check looks at a computer again. Nothing is changed.

8
00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:10.773
A server is reached from one of your computers. Reconnect signs in again, and you choose which computer does it.

9
00:01:11.488 --> 00:01:16.213
Add an environment asks what it is for and where it runs, then shows the app it found there.

10
00:01:22.489 --> 00:01:31.367
Nothing is saved before the review. When Save is off, it always says why. Here, Docker Compose is missing on that computer.

11
00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:41.134
What you started stays as a draft. At the top, the Releases switch pauses releases and automatic updates. Nothing that runs is stopped.

12
00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:43.982
Turn it on again when you are ready.

13
00:01:44.682 --> 00:01:49.430
That is Environments: set up where your app runs once, and release when you are ready.
